# Conformance probe pack for gate blocks with sentinels (spec 0.17, ruling 6).
# Fixed `bits` layout, least significant bit first. Public. No kinds. One
# byte per word. Exercises: the "invalid when 1" form, a gate of value 0 that
# holds on the zero bits of an entity without the key and so writes the
# sentinel; a block whose field holds its sentinel keeps its gate on
# re-encode when a raw key outside the blocks maps the gate bit (z, c1), and
# loses it when none does (w).
#
#   byte 0       bit 0: y is not valid when 1; bits 1-7: x, outside any block
#   byte 1       y, absent 255
#   byte 2       bit 16: z is valid, also the raw key c1
#   byte 3       z, absent 255
#   byte 4       bit 32: w is valid, no raw key
#   byte 5       w, absent 255
format     conformance-gates-absent
version    0.17.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses       probe
wire       bits
word_bytes 1
field   probe.x   0:1:7    uint
if      0:0:1  0
  field probe.y   0:8:8    uint  absent 255
end
field   probe.c1  0:16:1   uint
if      0:16:1 1
  field probe.z   0:24:8   uint  absent 255
end
if      0:32:1 1
  field probe.w   0:40:8   uint  absent 255
end
